Of course. To add a clickable "X" that deletes the variable tag, you'll need to modify three parts of your code:
 * The VariableBlot: Update its HTML structure to include a delete icon.
 * Your CSS: Add styles to position the "X" and make it appear on hover.
 * The EmailTemplate Component: Add a useEffect hook to listen for clicks on the delete icon and safely remove the blot using the Quill API.
1. Update the VariableBlot Definition
Modify the static create method to return a <span> that contains both the variable text and a dedicated <span> for the delete icon. We'll also add a class to the main node so we can target it easily.
// In VariableBlot, outside your component

class VariableBlot extends Embed {
  static create(value) {
    // The parent node that represents the entire blot
    const node = super.create();
    node.setAttribute('contenteditable', 'false');
    // Add a class for easier targeting
    node.classList.add('variable-blot');

    // Node for the variable's text
    const text = document.createElement('span');
    text.innerText = value;

    // Node for the delete button 'X'
    const closer = document.createElement('span');
    closer.innerText = 'X';
    // Add a class to identify the delete button
    closer.classList.add('variable-delete-icon');

    node.appendChild(text);
    node.appendChild(closer);

    // Apply styles to the main blot node
    Object.assign(node.style, {
      // Add position relative to position the 'X'
      position: 'relative',
      backgroundColor: '#0c476e',
      color: 'white',
      padding: '5px 20px 5px 8px', // Increase right padding for the 'X'
      borderRadius: '3px',
      fontWeight: 'bold',
      margin: '0 2px',
      cursor: 'default',
      userSelect: 'none',
      display: 'inline-block', // Ensures proper layout
    });
    
    return node;
  }

  static value(domNode) {
    // Return the text of the first child (the text span)
    return domNode.firstChild.innerText;
  }
}

VariableBlot.blotName = 'variable';
VariableBlot.tagName = 'span';

2. Add CSS for the Delete Icon
Add the following styles to your quill.css file. This will position the "X" inside the tag and only show it when the user hovers over the variable.
/* In your quill.css file */

/* The 'X' icon is hidden by default */
.variable-delete-icon {
  display: none;
  position: absolute;
  right: 5px;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  cursor: pointer;
  font-size: 12px;
  font-weight: bold;
  font-family: monospace;
}

/* On hover of the blot, show the 'X' and give a visual cue */
.variable-blot:hover {
  background-color: #d32f2f !important; /* Use !important to override inline style */
}

.variable-blot:hover .variable-delete-icon {
  display: inline-block;
}

3. Handle the Click Event to Delete the Blot
Finally, add a useEffect hook to your EmailTemplate component. This will attach a click listener to the editor only when it's in edit mode.
// In your EmailTemplate component

useEffect(() => {
  // Ensure we have a ref to the editor
  const editor = bodyEditorRef.current?.getEditor();
  if (!editor || !isEditing) return;

  // The function to handle clicks inside the editor
  const handleClick = (e) => {
    // Check if the clicked element is our delete icon
    if (e.target.classList.contains('variable-delete-icon')) {
      // Find the parent blot node
      const blotNode = e.target.closest('.variable-blot');
      if (blotNode) {
        // Use Quill's API to find the blot instance from the DOM node
        const blot = Quill.find(blotNode, true);
        if (blot) {
          // Get the blot's position and safely delete it
          const index = editor.getIndex(blot);
          editor.deleteText(index, blot.length(), 'user');
        }
      }
    }
  };

  // Add the listener
  editor.root.addEventListener('click', handleClick);

  // Cleanup: remove the listener when the component unmounts or exits edit mode
  return () => {
    editor.root.removeEventListener('click', handleClick);
  };
}, [isEditing]); // Rerun this effect whenever 'isEditing' changes

Now, when you are in "Edit" mode, hovering over a variable tag will reveal an "X". Clicking it will safely remove the entire tag from the editor.
